..0xFF`), NUL output byte, unchecked `setlocale`/`printf`, garbage-high-bit `int` across the FFI boundary, plus unprototyped-`main` extra arguments. All 20 rows + 2 generic rows have passing differential tests.\n- **CONFIGS.md** — 35 rows: the 16 distinct glibc class groups, exhaustive all-256 sweeps, batched multi-call sequences, `int`-prototype FFI shape, host locales (`en_US.iso88591` etc. must not leak), file/pipe stdin and stdout, >8 KiB stdin, repeated `main` calls consuming successive bytes, plus end-to-end executable comparisons. 0 unchecked rows.\n\n## Test suite (`tests/`, 69 tests)\nAll comparisons load **both** `.so`s with `libloading` and call the exported symbols in a freshly `fork()`ed child (isolated stdio/locale state), comparing stdout bytes, return values, exit code and termination signal. `harness_selfcheck.rs` proves the harness is non-vacuous (byte-exact 189-byte reference, detects differences, loads two genuinely different objects).\n\n## Configurations verified\n`Cargo.toml` declares no `[features]` and the CMake/C side has no `#ifdef`/options → one combination, exercised as both `default` and `--no-default-features`, under **debug and release** (`panic = \"abort\"`): `PROFILES=\"debug release\" ./verify.sh` → **ALL CONFIGURATIONS PASSED**, symbol parity confirmed for both profiles. Mutation tests (table entry, `tolower` entry, SIGPIPE fix) each produce failures, confirming the suite detects regressions."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":723,"cache_read_input_tokens":154119,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":723,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e616948-f566-4754-8206-510a7f088537","uuid":"ee6e27d6-6fe8-410d-86fb-ab81df8d0f88","timestamp":"2026-08-18T06:27:08.950Z"}
